# Allowlist .gitignore — ignore everything, then un-ignore deliberately.
#
# Rationale: a denylist leaks whatever you forget to name. An allowlist fails
# closed — a new file is invisible to git until someone adds a line for it. If
# `git status` doesn't show your new file, that is this file working as
# intended: add the un-ignore line below.
#
# This repo must be PUBLIC (GitHub Pages is only free on public repos), so
# everything tracked here is world-readable forever. Nothing secret gets an
# un-ignore line, and `scripts/secret_scan.sh` enforces that before every push.
#
# Git rule governing the ordering: you cannot re-include a file if one of its
# parent directories is excluded. So each tree is un-ignored as a directory
# first (`!/icons/`), then as contents (`!/icons/**`). Last matching pattern wins.

*

# --- Top-level files ---------------------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/.nvmrc
!/.env.example
!/README.md
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json

# --- The PWA (served at the repo root by GitHub Pages) -----------------------
!/index.html
!/app.js
!/styles.css
!/manifest.webmanifest
!/sw.js
!/icons/
!/icons/**

# --- Vendored libraries ------------------------------------------------------
# Committed rather than fetched from a CDN: no build step, and no third party
# whose outage takes the app down. Read before committing, like anything else.
!/vendor/
!/vendor/**

# --- Backend -----------------------------------------------------------------
!/backend/
!/backend/**
# ...but never clasp's credentials, which land inside backend/.
/backend/.clasp.json
/backend/.clasprc.json

# --- Supabase Edge Functions -------------------------------------------------
# Server-side code, deployed by hand with the Supabase CLI but version-controlled
# here like everything else.
#
# Only the .ts source is un-ignored, and the narrowness is the point: a blanket
# `!/supabase/functions/**` would out-rank the `.env` rule further down, and
# `supabase secrets set` writes exactly `supabase/functions/.env` — the file
# holding the Gemini key. The scanner would catch it by name, but a secret that
# git never sees cannot be committed by accident in the first place. The
# directory lines are needed too: git will not look inside a folder it has
# already excluded, so each level has to be let back in before the files are.
!/supabase/
!/supabase/functions/
!/supabase/functions/*/
!/supabase/functions/**/*.ts

# --- Tooling and docs --------------------------------------------------------
!/scripts/
!/scripts/**
!/docs/
!/docs/**

# --- The stage pipeline (agent definitions; no secrets) ----------------------
!/.claude/
!/.claude/**

# --- Noise -------------------------------------------------------------------
# These sit inside un-ignored trees, so they need re-ignoring explicitly.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# WSL writes these next to files copied from Windows.
*Zone.Identifier

# --- Deliberately NOT tracked ------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE.md   — describes this machine's setup; the repo is public.
# .env        — real token and API URL. Copy .env.example to .env and fill it in.
# node_modules/, .venv/, ~/.probeing/  — all covered by `*` above.
